<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- DERIVED FILE.  ur10_table's URDF, plus the round-5 flange force/torque
     cell and its calibration payload, and nothing else (R5_07 T-14, R5_08
     D-14).  `test_ur10_ft_urdf_is_the_base_urdf_plus_the_cell` asserts exactly
     that, so the two cannot drift.

     It is a separate asset rather than an edit of ur10_table because the
     calibration payload is 5 kg of permanent hardware at the flange, and the
     round-4 UR10 invariants are stated for a bare flange: three of them
     (C3's worst-case peak torque, C8's wrist-channel signal, C9's wrist_3
     anti-aliasing margin) fail outright if that mass is added to the asset
     they are written about.  Round 5 has kept every round-4 invariant it
     could; this is how it keeps these three. -->
